WEBVTT

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:36.650
When I open my photo book, I see different sides of me. {purichou...}

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:39.420
Laughing, {warattari}

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:42.200
or playing it cool, in all the pictures. {sumashitari de...}

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.930
I don't wanna say, "what's with all these characters?" But... {nani kore...}

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:47.640
Isn't this too much fun? {arisugi...}

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:50.220
For real? {maji...}

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:52.430
I mean, thanks! {tte yuu ka...}

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:55.760
Even if I lose my way,  {maigo ni...}

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:58.370
my heart's egg {kokoro no...}

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:01.140
will be all right. Come back {daijoubu...}

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:03.830
to me! {modotteoide}

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:06.610
Hey, when we're together... {kimi to...}

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:09.330
Hop, step, jump!

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:11.940
Because you're here... {kimi ga...}

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:14.590
Drew, draw, drawn!

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:17.460
I'm always with you...  {kimi to...}

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:20.180
Chip, syrup, whip!

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:22.860
One more time,  {mou ichido...}

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:25.470
unlock my heart! {kokoro...}

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:28.240
I love you.  {daisuki yo}

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:30.700
All of you.  {minna}

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:33.590
I want to be next to you. {soba ni...}

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:35.900
Okay? {ne...}

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:37.050
Love ya! {suki yo}

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:48.610
And so, taking all of the data into account,

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:53.820
the Embryo tends to appear whenever there is a large outbreak of X Eggs.

00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:55.390
Oh?

00:01:55.390 --> 00:01:56.100
And?

00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:57.780
Please take a look at this.

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:01.360
What is that?

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:03.620
It's the robot we've been designing.

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:10.000
We made it from the data my Yukari-senpai, and that Nikaidou guy, left us.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:13.110
It's powered by the X Egg's energy.

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:16.000
It uses radar to detect people with weak heart's eggs.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.770
Express, full-speed ahead!

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:20.350
So when exposed to the X Egg's energy, what happens?

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:23.350
An X Egg comes out of the child's heart!

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:25.560
It makes capturing them a cinch.

00:02:27.470 --> 00:02:30.890
With this robot, we can collect a multitude of them,

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:34.320
making it only a matter of time until we obtain the Embryo.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.200
Oh?

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:37.660
We've already given it a name, too.

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:39.220
Let's hear it.

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:40.840
We call it...

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:42.660
The Embryon!

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:48.850
Once the final checks are finished, we plan to do a field test using this prototype.

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:50.560
Go ahead, then.

00:02:53.050 --> 00:02:56.320
After all, we cannot stand idly by. {note, the japanese here is a tricky set phrase that literally means "with hands folded"}

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:59.190
The problem is Tsukiyomi Ikuto,

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:02.690
including his lack of reports on his progress in finding the Embryo.

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:06.600
What am I going to do about him?

00:03:07.390 --> 00:03:12.390
Episode 49
The Secret of the Violin! Notes Dancing on the Wind!

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:18.560
We didn't find the Embryo today either-nya.

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:19.470
Yeah.

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:23.710
Ikuto, are you honestly even looking for it?

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:25.160
What does it look like to you?

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:28.170
I'm not really sure-nya.

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:33.200
So, what are you going to wish for if you find it-nya?

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:35.140
That, right?

00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:41.170
What was that for?

00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:50.720
If you don't hurry up, your mom will get angry!

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:53.670
You hung around too long after the Guardians meeting.

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:00.150
What's that?

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:01.580
That sound...

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:02.970
Do you think it's...

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:15.810
I knew it. It's Ikuto.

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:22.570
I know that song.

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:28.120
I won't lose to anyone,

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:30.560
because I have a dream.

00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:33.790
It's like my-

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:37.470
I thought I heard someone, and it's you.

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:40.160
Sounds like you're having a fun time singing-nya.

00:04:40.690 --> 00:04:44.400
I'm n-not really having all that much fun.

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:47.410
Anyway, I haven't seen you lately.

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:49.830
Have you been hanging around somewhere else?

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:51.280
You've got perfect timing.

00:04:52.230 --> 00:04:54.970
I was just getting bored.

00:04:54.970 --> 00:04:58.900
I'd be glad to have your crappy singing accompany me.

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:00.360
Crappy?

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:00.810
Let's go.

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:02.400
One, two, three!

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:03.120
Go!

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:06.880
Somebody sing a song.

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:12.090
Raise your head and open your heart.

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:15.910
Sing.

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:22.970
You can't give up.

00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:28.010
There's nothing you can't do.

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:34.620
Song of courage.

00:05:35.030 --> 00:05:39.160
I won't lose to anyone,

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:41.690
because I have a dream.

00:05:42.890 --> 00:05:47.120
It's like my heart's set off on a journey.

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:51.140
There's a path that exists only for me.

00:05:51.140 --> 00:05:54.270
I believe-

00:05:56.070 --> 00:05:58.330
A string broke-nya.

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:01.570
Maybe it was because of your singing, Amu-chan?

00:06:01.570 --> 00:06:02.260
No way!

00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:04.580
Super voice sound wave!

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:05.620
Could be.

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:11.730
Damn, I'm out of spare strings.

00:06:11.730 --> 00:06:13.170
Oh well, guess I've no choice.

00:06:13.170 --> 00:06:14.770
What'll you do?

00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:20.860
This is...

00:06:28.890 --> 00:06:30.190
My,

00:06:30.190 --> 00:06:31.710
if it isn't Ikuto.

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:32.990
It's been a while.

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:34.520
A string broke.

00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:35.890
Let me see.

00:06:35.890 --> 00:06:39.580
Wow, amazing! They're so artistic!

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:42.410
Are you Ikuto's girlfriend?

00:06:42.410 --> 00:06:44.080
N-No!

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:46.760
So even Ikuto's at the age to have a girlfriend, huh?

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:48.580
I said I'm not!

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:50.850
The same gut string as usual?

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:51.560
Yeah.

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:54.580
No one's listening.

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:57.630
Kotone, please bring the customers some tea!

00:06:57.630 --> 00:06:58.810
Okay!

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:02.200
The tail piece is a bit loose.

00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:03.640
I'll go ahead and fix it.

00:07:07.770 --> 00:07:10.220
Ikuto-san! It's been so long!

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:11.770
Have you grown even taller?

00:07:11.770 --> 00:07:12.520
Maybe.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:15.190
Kotone.

00:07:15.190 --> 00:07:16.970
Hurry up and serve the tea.

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:18.920
And don't forget Ikuto's girlfriend.

00:07:19.670 --> 00:07:21.720
Girlfriend?

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:25.870
Pleased-to-meet-you.

00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:28.920
I keep saying I'm not!

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:32.630
Oh, so you're not his girlfriend!

00:07:32.630 --> 00:07:35.200
You should have told me sooner.

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:37.430
I said it right at the start.

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:39.130
By the way, Kotone...

00:07:39.130 --> 00:07:42.110
We have another customer coming today.

00:07:42.110 --> 00:07:43.360
Another one?

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:45.660
Yes, it's Honda Saeko-san.

00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:46.890
Saeko-san?

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:48.900
Who's that?

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:52.620
A famous violinist who's used our shop for a long time.

00:07:53.630 --> 00:07:54.740
There we go.

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:56.390
Ikuto,

00:07:56.390 --> 00:07:57.720
try playing it for me.

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:15.380
Seems like there aren't any problems.

00:08:15.380 --> 00:08:17.420
I'll be in the inner workshop,

00:08:17.420 --> 00:08:19.550
so please call me when Saeko-san arrives.

00:08:19.550 --> 00:08:20.060
Right.

00:08:21.650 --> 00:08:25.770
Your dad fixed the violin just like that.

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:29.140
Well, that's because making them is his job.

00:08:29.140 --> 00:08:31.560
Really? He can make violins?

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:33.070
Of course.

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:37.830
Even Ikuto's violin was made by someone like my dad.

00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:44.310
Violins can't produce a good sound right after they're made, you see.

00:08:44.740 --> 00:08:46.930
Though each one is different,

00:08:46.930 --> 00:08:51.570
it can take fifty, a hundred, or even two hundred years for it to produce its best sound.

00:08:51.820 --> 00:08:53.280
A hundred years?

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:55.370
Then, you couldn't even hear it yourself!

00:08:55.370 --> 00:08:56.290
That's right.

00:08:56.290 --> 00:09:03.000
But you know, I think the people who made the rare and famous violins were just like us.

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:08.770
They hoped they'd become great instruments after a hundred or two hundred years,

00:09:08.770 --> 00:09:10.620
and made them with that in mind.

00:09:11.680 --> 00:09:14.390
I want to become a craftsman like that.

00:09:15.670 --> 00:09:17.430
It's so romantic!

00:09:17.860 --> 00:09:22.460
But Dad hasn't started to teach me very much yet.

00:09:22.460 --> 00:09:25.170
So I've been studying on my own in secret.

00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:29.410
Good evening.

00:09:29.410 --> 00:09:30.940
Saeko-san!

00:09:32.020 --> 00:09:35.090
Kotone-chan. My, how you've grown.

00:09:35.090 --> 00:09:37.530
Has it really been two years?

00:09:37.530 --> 00:09:38.910
I think so.

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:41.670
Wait here, I'll call my father for you.

00:09:41.670 --> 00:09:43.020
It's okay.

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:46.000
He's busy with something else, right?

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:47.530
I don't want to bother him.

00:09:48.360 --> 00:09:51.230
I'd like to have this violin adjusted, please.

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:54.110
I need it before I leave for Paris.

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:55.090
Sure.

00:09:55.090 --> 00:09:57.660
And I have one more for you to take care of.

00:10:00.510 --> 00:10:01.890
Kotone-chan,

00:10:01.890 --> 00:10:03.600
would you do this one yourself?

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:08.250
I'm asking you,

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:10.520
as a future violin craftsman.

00:10:16.900 --> 00:10:19.790
Wow, you got a request for a job!

00:10:19.790 --> 00:10:20.430
Yeah.

00:10:20.430 --> 00:10:22.070
I'm leaving.

00:10:22.070 --> 00:10:23.910
Give my best to your old man.

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:26.500
What do you think? Can I really do it?

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:28.790
They're ignoring us.

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:28.570
It'll be fine.

00:10:28.570 --> 00:10:31.060
But it's an important violin. Yeah, I've got to do it.

00:10:28.790 --> 00:10:30.120
Just leave them be.

00:10:31.060 --> 00:10:31.650
Yeah!

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:32.940
I'll have to do my best.

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:34.650
Right. Good luck!

00:10:38.140 --> 00:10:41.060
Hey, can I come back tomorrow to see it?

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:02.050
Done!

00:11:02.050 --> 00:11:04.640
We've finally completed the Embryon!

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:06.500
Indeed, we did!

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:09.130
It's the fruit of our combined efforts!

00:11:09.130 --> 00:11:11.160
Let's hurry up and test it out.

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:12.030
Right!

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:16.150
This is currently one of our last X Eggs.

00:11:16.150 --> 00:11:19.230
However! If our Embryon works as we designed it,

00:11:19.230 --> 00:11:22.030
that shouldn't be a problem for long!

00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:34.760
It's floating!

00:11:34.760 --> 00:11:36.540
Chief, you did it!

00:11:36.540 --> 00:11:39.120
Go, Embryon!

00:11:44.040 --> 00:11:45.350
Hello.

00:11:51.790 --> 00:11:54.580
She's been like this the whole time.

00:11:54.580 --> 00:11:57.980
She's been working at it non-stop, without even eating.

00:12:04.330 --> 00:12:06.660
Pretty amazing concentration there, don't you think?

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:07.660
No kidding.

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:08.680
But...

00:12:08.680 --> 00:12:10.480
This is boring.

00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:11.850
It sure is.

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:30.000
Oh, I see. So that's it.

00:12:34.180 --> 00:12:36.100
All right!

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:37.160
I've finished!

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:44.790
But I suddenly feel kind of...

00:13:02.640 --> 00:13:05.180
Oh, you're done.

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:07.340
Sorry. Did I wake you?

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:09.320
No, I'm fine.

00:13:09.320 --> 00:13:12.390
Anyway, look at this, I did it myself.

00:13:14.380 --> 00:13:15.670
What happened?

00:13:18.490 --> 00:13:20.470
I spilled the tea,

00:13:20.470 --> 00:13:23.200
and the glue came undone.

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:25.180
What? What do you mean?

00:13:25.180 --> 00:13:29.000
What'll I do? Saeko-san's coming to pick it up tonight!

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:30.940
Why don't you ask your dad?

00:13:30.940 --> 00:13:33.170
There might be some way to fix it.

00:13:33.170 --> 00:13:38.040
I can't! A mistake like this says I'm a failure as a violin craftsman!

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:38.950
But...

00:13:42.650 --> 00:13:44.360
Ah, hello.

00:13:44.360 --> 00:13:46.130
Yes, sure.

00:13:47.060 --> 00:13:49.740
Kotone, Saeko-san's on the phone for you.

00:13:51.020 --> 00:13:52.540
Kotone-san!

00:13:53.550 --> 00:13:54.810
Wait!

00:13:55.410 --> 00:13:56.540
Kotone?

00:13:57.970 --> 00:13:59.520
Huh?

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:01.260
Kotone-san!

00:14:02.550 --> 00:14:04.440
I wonder where she went.

00:14:04.440 --> 00:14:06.570
Amu-chan, over there!

00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:07.820
You can tell?

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:11.670
We can sense Kotone-san's heart's egg!

00:14:11.670 --> 00:14:13.900
But it's feeling worse and worse.

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:15.720
Let's hurry!

00:14:19.260 --> 00:14:20.920
I can

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:22.800
never be a violin craftsman.

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:38.540
An X Egg?

00:14:41.720 --> 00:14:43.060
It's getting away!

00:14:46.600 --> 00:14:47.760
Ikuto!

00:14:50.520 --> 00:14:53.560
Aw man, this isn't the Embryo-nya.

00:14:53.560 --> 00:14:55.960
Just throw away that trash already.

00:14:55.960 --> 00:14:58.010
Don't! That's not trash!

00:14:58.010 --> 00:15:00.770
It's Kotone-san's heart's egg!

00:15:00.770 --> 00:15:02.310
Kotone's...

00:15:04.930 --> 00:15:09.340
Trill, Tremolo, Pizzicato!

00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:11.100
It became an X Character!

00:15:15.360 --> 00:15:17.060
Miki, let's Character Transform!

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:17.390
Right!

00:15:19.890 --> 00:15:21.490
My heart:

00:15:21.490 --> 00:15:22.780
Unlock!

00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:38.680
Character Transformation: Amulet Spade!

00:15:38.680 --> 00:15:41.060
Trill!

00:15:47.570 --> 00:15:50.600
I'm not cut out to be a violin craftsman!

00:15:50.600 --> 00:15:52.680
I have no talent!

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:54.420
What are you talking about?

00:15:54.420 --> 00:15:57.310
Stradivarius!

00:16:00.030 --> 00:16:01.450
Amu-chan!

00:16:01.450 --> 00:16:03.970
Hey, help us out, you guys!

00:16:03.970 --> 00:16:05.450
What are you blabbing about-nya?

00:16:05.450 --> 00:16:08.780
Did you forget? We're enemies!

00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:10.880
Man, you lazy jerk!

00:16:10.880 --> 00:16:12.680
Amu-chan, fight!

00:16:13.970 --> 00:16:15.640
Tremolo!

00:16:20.510 --> 00:16:23.590
I spoke so confidently, but then I screwed up so bad!

00:16:23.590 --> 00:16:26.650
I can never show my face to my dad or Saeko-san!

00:16:30.790 --> 00:16:32.310
What are you saying?

00:16:32.310 --> 00:16:34.270
Who cares if you screw up once or twice?

00:16:35.850 --> 00:16:37.970
A hundred years... Two hundred years...

00:16:37.970 --> 00:16:41.720
That's a dream I can't even imagine!

00:16:41.720 --> 00:16:43.380
So what if it's a little over-the-top? {the translation of "erasouna" here is tricky... literally it's "speaking from a place you don't deserve to be in", or haughty, but here it's referring to kotone talking about her work possibly being something great 200 years from now...}

00:16:43.380 --> 00:16:44.100
But...

00:16:45.470 --> 00:16:47.830
When you were telling me about your dream,

00:16:47.830 --> 00:16:49.740
I thought you were really cool.

00:16:49.740 --> 00:16:51.680
You were dazzling.

00:16:51.680 --> 00:16:55.200
You should always hold on to that lofty dream!

00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:57.220
Amu-chan!

00:16:58.640 --> 00:17:00.470
Negative Heart:

00:17:02.390 --> 00:17:03.950
Lock On!

00:17:08.790 --> 00:17:10.680
Open Heart!

00:17:24.510 --> 00:17:26.850
Thank you, Amu-chan.

00:17:26.850 --> 00:17:28.850
I have faith in Kotone-chan.

00:17:28.850 --> 00:17:33.830
I know she'll create violins people will think are amazing hundreds of years from now!

00:17:40.060 --> 00:17:41.260
What was I...

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:45.680
Let's hurry back to the workshop.

00:17:45.680 --> 00:17:47.220
We have to fix the violin.

00:17:48.660 --> 00:17:49.610
Right.

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:54.160
Can't we just have Su fix it?

00:17:54.160 --> 00:17:56.770
That's right! If we use Remake Honey, then...

00:17:56.770 --> 00:17:59.670
Just leave fixing things to me!

00:17:59.670 --> 00:18:01.050
But that would be...

00:18:01.050 --> 00:18:04.280
Not that I care if you fix it that way, but...

00:18:05.580 --> 00:18:09.310
If Kotone doesn't do it herself, is there even a point?

00:18:10.550 --> 00:18:13.980
Amu-chan, I'm going to hurry back to the workshop.

00:18:14.770 --> 00:18:15.960
Oh, okay.

00:18:18.800 --> 00:18:20.110
Ikuto.

00:18:30.150 --> 00:18:31.340
Dad.

00:18:32.310 --> 00:18:34.060
Dad, I'm sorry!

00:18:36.780 --> 00:18:38.890
You know, violins

00:18:38.890 --> 00:18:40.830
are instruments that can break.

00:18:42.410 --> 00:18:47.280
Craftsmen from both long ago and today all think the same way.

00:18:47.800 --> 00:18:51.090
They don't focus on making an instrument that will never break.

00:18:51.090 --> 00:18:54.150
When that happens, our job as craftsmen is to fix it. {Wow, what a racket they have :) sounds like american car companies}

00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:59.410
The musician performs, and the craftsman does the maintenance.

00:18:59.410 --> 00:19:02.410
If it gets damaged, we fix it,

00:19:02.410 --> 00:19:05.150
and the violin becomes even stronger.

00:19:06.940 --> 00:19:08.470
Dad.

00:19:19.960 --> 00:19:21.470
Hello.

00:19:24.950 --> 00:19:26.660
It's wonderful.

00:19:27.160 --> 00:19:28.810
Thank you very much.

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:31.910
And what about the one I asked you to look after, Kotone-chan?

00:19:33.780 --> 00:19:35.180
Here it is.

00:19:39.940 --> 00:19:44.880
I'm sorry! Because of my carelessness, the top board came undone.

00:19:44.880 --> 00:19:46.710
I tried to fix it,

00:19:46.710 --> 00:19:48.430
but I couldn't finish in time.

00:19:48.950 --> 00:19:51.760
You tried to fix it yourself?

00:19:51.760 --> 00:19:53.140
Yes.

00:19:53.140 --> 00:19:55.360
Did you consult your dad about it?

00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:56.050
Yes.

00:19:56.850 --> 00:19:59.870
But you asked me to handle it,

00:19:59.870 --> 00:20:02.970
so I wanted to finish it myself.

00:20:09.550 --> 00:20:12.280
I have no doubt you'll become a great craftsman.

00:20:13.890 --> 00:20:17.890
You put your heart into this violin.

00:20:17.890 --> 00:20:20.730
And you know, even if it was damaged,

00:20:20.730 --> 00:20:22.930
it'll still produce a sound that'll pierce hearts.

00:20:23.280 --> 00:20:25.950
That's right, just like a person.

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:31.180
Even when you're hurt or frustrated, you overcome those feelings.

00:20:31.180 --> 00:20:34.670
And when you do, that's how you gain strength.

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:37.540
And that's how violins became wonderful instruments.

00:20:39.630 --> 00:20:44.110
Saeko-san, would you let me keep that violin for a while?

00:20:44.110 --> 00:20:45.890
Please let me fix it!

00:20:47.760 --> 00:20:49.170
I understand.

00:20:49.170 --> 00:20:49.970
Please go ahead.

00:20:50.870 --> 00:20:52.100
I will!

00:20:52.100 --> 00:20:54.660
Good for you! That's great!

00:20:54.660 --> 00:20:55.780
Thank you.

00:20:55.780 --> 00:21:01.240
My memories aren't completely clear, but I get the feeling you helped me out earlier.

00:21:01.240 --> 00:21:03.810
Or was that a dream?

00:21:03.810 --> 00:21:05.110
Could be.

00:21:05.110 --> 00:21:08.830
Wait, maybe Ikuto actually...

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:11.240
Oh, he is just so wonderful!

00:21:11.240 --> 00:21:14.730
I really do love him.

00:21:16.350 --> 00:21:18.240
What am I saying?

00:21:24.600 --> 00:21:26.820
Chief, I'm getting an egg signal!

00:21:26.820 --> 00:21:27.980
Really?

00:21:27.980 --> 00:21:30.140
I'll put up the Embryon's camera.

00:21:38.970 --> 00:21:42.200
Hey, what do you think you're doing with my merchandise?

00:21:42.200 --> 00:21:44.560
What's going on?

00:21:44.560 --> 00:21:45.510
No clue.

00:21:47.280 --> 00:21:48.690
The transmission has...

00:21:48.690 --> 00:21:49.910
Stopped.

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:51.100
Rats.

00:21:54.550 --> 00:21:57.040
Ikuto was right.

00:21:57.040 --> 00:22:01.970
Making your dreams come true is about overcoming various things.

00:22:01.970 --> 00:22:05.770
I've got to try hard, just like Kotone-san!

00:22:05.770 --> 00:22:07.470
What are you going to try hard for?

00:22:07.710 --> 00:22:08.810
Ikuto?

00:22:08.810 --> 00:22:10.300
Fight, Amu-chan!

00:22:10.300 --> 00:22:11.760
That's right, fight on!

00:22:11.760 --> 00:22:14.870
Hey. That's not it!

00:22:35.760 --> 00:22:42.730
There's no limit to the dreams we wild things can see.  {abarenbou...}

00:22:42.730 --> 00:22:43.870
(Yeah, yeah, yeah.)

00:22:43.870 --> 00:22:47.080
If we're born with 100% possibilities,  {kanouseo...}

00:22:47.080 --> 00:22:50.030
then let's keep livin' at 100%. {hyakupa...}

00:22:50.500 --> 00:22:54.870
Let's cry and laugh, {naritari...}

00:22:54.870 --> 00:22:58.490
and meet all kinds of people.  {ironna...}

00:22:58.490 --> 00:23:02.030
Let's discover what's precious, {daiji na}

00:23:02.030 --> 00:23:05.040
and even lose it. {nakushitari}

00:23:05.040 --> 00:23:05.790
(But don't worry.) {hai donmai...}

00:23:05.790 --> 00:23:09.410
We've just gotta keep on runnin', {gan gan...}

00:23:09.410 --> 00:23:12.200
because that way's the most fun, you see.  {sono hou...}

00:23:12.200 --> 00:23:13.120
(Right on, right on.)

00:23:13.120 --> 00:23:16.560
I wanna do this, and I wanna do that too. {are mo shitai...}

00:23:16.560 --> 00:23:17.500
Let's go!  (Go!!)  {iku...}

00:23:17.500 --> 00:23:18.540
Move out! (Yeah!!) {susu...}

00:23:18.540 --> 00:23:20.780
Let's do it with gusto! {gachinko de ...}

00:23:20.780 --> 00:23:27.410
Because there's only one you in this world, {sekai ni...}

00:23:27.410 --> 00:23:34.570
you've gotta make sure you find the things you love. {daisuki...}

00:23:50.330 --> 00:23:54.510
Commoners! I, your King, have finally found the Embryo!

00:23:54.510 --> 00:23:55.990
That's our Kiseki!

00:23:55.990 --> 00:23:59.340
We will therefore begin our Embryo capturing plan!

00:23:59.340 --> 00:24:00.120
All right!

00:24:00.120 --> 00:24:00.790
First, we-

00:24:00.790 --> 00:24:03.640
But instead of capturing it, maybe could befriend it? {check this line, I can't hear it properly}

00:24:03.640 --> 00:24:06.110
Once we catch it, we have to put it in this jar.

00:24:05.100 --> 00:24:07.640
What should I pack for lunch?

00:24:07.640 --> 00:24:10.480
Hey, you guys, take this seriously!

00:24:10.480 --> 00:24:11.970
Next time on Shugo Chara:

00:24:11.970 --> 00:24:14.080
We Actually Found It!? The Embryo!

00:24:14.080 --> 00:24:15.810
I wonder if we'll really find it.

00:24:15.810 --> 00:24:17.830
It'll be fine, as long as we have fun.

00:24:17.830 --> 00:24:18.390
Yeah, that's true.

00:24:18.390 --> 00:24:19.720
Hey!
